{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"promptId":"99f21099-1bdf-4e90-9d41-1443256357f6","agentId":"a37f3a34aafca097d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"You are a careful research engineer verifying that a sprint writeup's claimed numbers actually match the code and data, and that the experiments measure what the writeup says they measure. Be precise and concrete.\n\nREAD:\n- Writeup: /Users/dmitrymanning-coe/Documents/Research/FRA/fra_proj/experiments/fra_win/summary.md\n- Code: /Users/dmitrymanning-coe/Documents/Research/FRA/fra_proj/experiments/fra_win/jobs/j4_baselines.py, j5_locality.py, j6_robust.py, j7_keyside.py, j8_pareto.py\n- Data (JSON outputs): /tmp/fra_out/fra_win/out/j4/j4.json, j5/j5.json, j6/j6.json, j7/j7.json, j8/j8.json\n- FRA method: /Users/dmitrymanning-coe/Documents/Research/FRA/fra_proj/fra/core/fra.py\n\nVERIFY EACH OF THESE, citing the exact code line / json value:\n1. The writeup says \"at matched 50% suppression, FRA 0.14±0.03 vs ActAdd-identity 3.4±1.6 vs ActAdd prev-was-cue 3.0±0.8 nats\". Confirm these come from j8.json and that j8 actually interpolates collateral at the SAME suppression value for all three methods (not at each method's own max). Check the collat_at() interpolation logic.\n2. The writeup says j5: off-target KL 0.62 (FRA) vs 7.64 (ActAdd) at matched suppression (12×), and held-out \" war\"×5 text KL 0.13 vs 31 (235×). Confirm against j5.json and the j5 code. Check that \"matched suppression\" is actually enforced in j5 part 1.\n3. The writeup says j7: FRA beats both linear baselines ~16× on total held-out KL (0.14 vs 2.28 vs 2.18). Confirm against j7.json.\n4. Confirm the FRA intervention is what the writeup claims: a content-addressed subtraction of specific (query-feature,key-feature) bilinear score contributions from the induction heads' hook_attn_scores. Check pairs_delta() and the score-patch hook in j8/j5.\n5. Confirm the KL collateral is computed correctly (KL(clean||patched), correct sign, summed/meaned over positions as claimed).\n6. Confirm the ActAdd baselines are genuine linear residual steers (subtract a unit direction scaled by local norm at resid_pre), and that \"cue-identity\" vs \"prev-was-cue\" directions are constructed as described.\n7. Flag ANY discrepancy between a number in summary.md and the underlying json/code, and any place where the code does something different from what the writeup says.\n\nOUTPUT: a checklist (✓ verified / ✗ discrepancy / ⚠ caveat) for each item above, with the specific code line or json value as evidence. List any number in the writeup that you could NOT reproduce from the data. Do not modify any files."},"uuid":"e6866bdf-d1b9-454c-965a-13c336759af8","timestamp":"2026-06-10T08:20:44.691Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/dmitrymanning-coe/Documents/Research/FRA/fra_proj/experiments/fra_win","sessionId":"8a660228-bde0-4e60-bfe2-aafb33fe0b4d","version":"2.1.170","gitBranch":"autoresearch/fra-behavioral-win","slug":"moonlit-churning-gem"}
